    "q-216298": {
      "dom_id": "step-q216298",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "The exact distance between the points $(3,6)$ and $(2,-4)$ is{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "In this case, we have ${{(3,6)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{1})}$ and ${{(2,-4)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{2})}.$ \nSo, the distance $d$ can be calculated using the distance formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\sqrt{({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})^{2}+({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2-3)^{2}+(-4-6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+(-10)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+100} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{101}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
