    "q-216300": {
      "dom_id": "step-q216300",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "The distance between the points $(5,1)$ and $(1,-2)$ is{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "In this case, we have ${{(5,1)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{1})}$ and ${{(1,-2)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{2})}.$ \nSo, the distance $d$ can be calculated using the distance formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\sqrt{({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})^{2}+({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(1-5)^{2}+(-2-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
